  "name": "Haudenosaunee social dance songs (Eskanye, Smoke Dance and water-drum songs)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Social dance repertoire of the Six Nations, sung at socials in longhouses and community halls at Six Nations of the Grand River, Allegany, Cattaraugus, Akwesasne and other communities: the women's shuffle dance (Eskanye), Standing Quiver, Rabbit, Alligator, Fish and Smoke dances among many others. A lead singer plays the small wooden water drum and the other singers accompany him on cow-horn rattles, singing in unison or answering his phrases. A hand-drum card stands in for the water drum and a generic shaker card for the horn rattles.",
